-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`; every error code has a message in both.
+
+The server answers in the language the request's `Accept-Language` header
+prefers: the supported language with the highest q-value wins (the first
+listed on a tie), region tags such as `ko-KR` count as their language, and
+`q=0` refuses a language. Without the header, or when it names neither
+language (or only `*`), the server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (`en` or `ko`,
+default `en`).
